/// How many cells text occupies in a fixed-width grid, such as a terminal.
///
/// Most characters take one cell. East Asian wide and fullwidth characters and most emoji take two.
/// Combining marks, joiners, other zero-width characters and control characters take none.
/// <fn String.displayWidth> is the way to ask this of a string.
module Darklang.Stdlib.Wcwidth

/// Every codepoint from one start up to the next has that start's width. Upstream keeps a zero-width
/// table, a wide table and a few hand-picked zero-width characters; here they are merged into one
/// list, so a lookup is one binary search. Surrogates are skipped, since a string never holds one.
